{
  "mn141:0.1": "Middle Discourses 141 ",
  "mn141:0.2": "The Analysis of the Truths ",
  "mn141:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn141:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Varanasi in the deer park at Isipatana. ",
  "mn141:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn141:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn141:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn141:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn141:2.1": "“Near Varanasi, in the deer park at Isipatana, the Realized One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha rolled forth the supreme Wheel of Dhamma. And that wheel cannot be rolled back by any ascetic or brahmin or god or Māra or divinity or by anyone in the world. ",
  "mn141:2.2": "It is the teaching, advocating, establishing, clarifying, analyzing, and revealing of the four noble truths. ",
  "mn141:2.3": "What four? ",
  "mn141:3.1": "The noble truths of suffering, the origin of suffering, the cessation of suffering, and the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering. ",
  "mn141:4.1": "Near Varanasi, in the deer park at Isipatana, the Realized One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha rolled forth the supreme Wheel of Dhamma. And that wheel cannot be rolled back by any ascetic or brahmin or god or Māra or divinity or by anyone in the world. ",
  "mn141:4.2": "It is the teaching, advocating, establishing, clarifying, analyzing, and revealing of the four noble truths. ",
  "mn141:5.1": "Mendicants, you should cultivate friendship with Sāriputta and Moggallāna